2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
“relevant work experience”, in relation to an Environmental Control Officer, means practical experience in any of the following areas of work:
(a)cleaning services;
(b)environmental engineering;
(c)environmental health;
(d)estate management;
(e)pest control;
(f)waste management;
(g)any other area that, in the opinion of the Director‑General, is within the scope of an Environmental Control Officer’s duties under the Act;
“specified construction site” means any construction site to which section 62 of the Act applies;
“specified premises” means any premises or class of premises designated under section 62A(2) of the Act as specified premises.
